            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 516)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Review packages can't arrive with the wrong colour baked in.</b> The playback media inside a package carries a note saying which log curve it was encoded through, and Asobi undoes that curve to show you the picture. It was possible for that note to say "ACEScct" on a file that had never been converted — which played back looking wrong with nothing to explain it. The app that builds packages now refuses rather than shipping one.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
